	(gr_text "FLEX ELECTRODE PCB - FABRICATION NOTES\n========================================\n\nCONSTRUCTION\n------------\nSingle-layer flex, polyimide substrate, 18µm (0.5oz) copper, \npolyimide coverlay both sides, except:\n  - electrode contact area (comb array) - see below\n  - wire-solder pads at pigtail tip - see below\n\nLAYER COUNT (KiCad file only)\n------------------------------\nThe KiCad file shows 2 copper layers (F.Cu / B.Cu). This is only \nbecause KiCad requires an even number of copper layers and has no \n{dblquote}1 layer{dblquote} option. B.Cu and B.Mask are unused, empty, and excluded \nfrom the Gerber output. The actual manufactured part is single-layer.\n\nELECTRODE FINISH\n----------------\nElectrode contact finish: ENIG\nLeave exposed - no coverlay/soldermask over this area.\n\nWIRE-SOLDER PADS\n-----------------\nWire-solder pads at pigtail tip: leave exposed (no coverlay).\nWire connection.\n\nPIGTAIL TAIL\n------------\nTail width: 1.5mm\nDesigned to pass through an endoscope working channel - keep this \nsection as slim and flexible as possible. No stiffener along its length.\n\nSTIFFENER\n---------\nRequested: thin, flexible polyimide stiffener (NOT FR4/glass), bonded \nto underside of solder-pad area only, at the pigtail tip.\nPurpose: reinforce the solder joint against flex/handling stress at \nthe wire termination point - this is not part of the 4.5mm main bend, \njust local reinforcement at the rigid solder joint.\nPlease advise on suitable stiffener material/thickness given our \nstackup, and include as an added process step if feasible.\n\nBEND RADIUS / USE CASE\n-----------------------\nMinimum bend radius in service: 4.5mm, static bend (board is wrapped \nonce around a 9mm OD cylinder, not repeatedly flexed).\n\nBIOCOMPATIBILITY\n-----------------\nPrototype for autonomous control system testing - no patient contact. \nStandard flex materials/finishes are fine; no biocompatibility \nrequirement at this stage.\n\nDRC / UNCONNECTED COPPER NOTE\n-------------------------------\nDRC {dblquote}unconnected{dblquote} warnings on comb electrode fingers and other custom \ncopper shapes are expected and have been excluded in the design file. \nConnectivity is completed physically by a piezoresistive film bonded \nover the electrode area, not by copper trace. This has been verified \nvisually - the shapes were hand-drawn rather than netlist-linked pads.\n\nQUESTION FOR YOUR APPLICATIONS ENGINEER\n------------------------------------------\nPlease confirm the coverlay openings over the electrode comb and \nsolder pads will result in fully bare exposed copper, not a thinned \nresidual coverlay film, given the small size of these openings.\n\nPlease also confirm overall stackup thickness is compatible with a \n4.5mm static bend radius for this application."
		(at 95.26 151.93 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "02e1b17c-f067-4b88-9e9c-130b1eb7395f")
